import subprocess
from Bio import Blast, SeqIO

subprocess.run(["blastn", "-query", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_ref.ffn", "-db", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/geneDatabase", "-perc_identity", "70", "-qcov_hsp_perc", "70", "-outfmt", "5", "-max_target_seqs", "10000", "10000", "-num_threads", "8", "-out", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_hits.xml",])

allMatches = Blast.read("/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_hits.xml")

bestHit = {}

for hit in allMatches:
        valueGene = hit.target.description
        keyGenome = valueGene.split("__")[0]
        if keyGenome not in bestHit:
                bestHit[keyGenome] = valueGene

topHitNames = set(bestHit.values())
topHitSequences = []
for gene in SeqIO.parse("/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/allGenes.ffn", "fasta"):
        if gene.id not in topHitNames:
                continue
        if len(gene.seq) % 3 != 0:
                continue
        if str(gene.seq)[-3:] in ["TAA", "TAG", "TGA"]:
                gene.seq = gene.seq[:-3]
        if "*" in gene.seq.translate():
                continue
        topHitSequences.append(gene)
SeqIO.write(topHitSequences[:100], "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/allTopHitsNhaA.ffn", "fasta")

subprocess.run(["macse", "-prog", "alignSequences", "-seq", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/allTopHitsNhaA.ffn", "-out_NT", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_aligned.fasta",])

subprocess.run(["FastTree", "-nt", "-gtr", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_aligned.fasta"],stdout=open("/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_tree.nwk", "w"),)

subprocess.run(["hyphy", "fel","--alignment", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_aligned.fasta","--tree", "/home/bahar/danssaltgenes/nhaA_tree.nwk",])


Some problems that I have encountered, fixed, or will fix in the future:
- I wish to find a manner to grab the sequence and store it rather than scanning all of the DB again. My combined IDs were over the 50 character limit, so we had to drop -parse_squids that would be able to directly grab each gene directly.
- Because of the above bullt point, it will be much harder to reproduce this code efficiently for other salt genes that we want to analyze. Therefore, I will try to generalize the code in the future to make it more reproducible.
- Clustalo is not codon aware, so after the alignment, it new stop codons would generate in the middle of the sequence. Therefore, I turned to macse.
- Beacuse of the above bullet point, I only ran the code for the first 100 genenes (SeqIO.write(topHitSequences[:100],....), because macse was a bit slow and I was worried I would not have time to present data for this week's meeting.
- Next time, I will try to see how efficient macse would be with all of the genomes.
- If needed, I can potentially adjust the criteria that I used for the inital BLAST (70/70).
